-- title:
--   Caccetta–Häggkvist for $r = 3$
-- statement:
--   **The rung $r=3$ of the Caccetta–Häggkvist conjecture** (Hamidoune, 1987). Every loopless digraph on $n\ge 1$ vertices in which every vertex has out-degree at least $3$ contains a directed cycle of length at most $\lceil n/3\rceil$:
--
--   $$\delta^+(D)\ge 3 \implies \text{girth}(D)\le\lceil n/3\rceil .$$
-- source:
--   Y. O. Hamidoune, A note on minimal directed graphs with given girth, JCTB 43 (1987), 343–348, https://doi.org/10.1016/0095-8956(87)90009-8

import Definitions.Def_TenChallenges_Challenge_03

